 ## Review and timing obligations
 
 Every completed level publishes the final FUR, response pairs including final acknowledgement, reconstructable patches, manifest, actual model/effort/session provenance, finding dispositions, changed calls and open choices. Native originals and qualified timing anchors remain available; private credentials/handles are excluded. A five-round cap with unresolved required findings is not acceptance.
 
-M1 owns review open, live provisional review turn, review complete and final import/validation, as well as the portable v0 adapter and migration. Between M1 and M4, the coordinator opens a level through core before review, ingests each submitted manual/native response and available public timing anchors, completes the bundle, and uses the core writer for final FUR import. Missing native claim/start evidence stays Unknown until a public source supports it. M4 owns the no-precommit record-only producer, automatic true per-turn starts where supported and automatic handoff to that existing sink. Planning time is recorded by story/state/level/role/model but never feeds trips. Registration time reused across native rounds is not per-turn engagement; claim/prior-submit bounds, unknown spans, setup and publication exclusions remain explicit. Backfill names and hashes its sources, deduplicates turns and does not manufacture observations. Live and backfilled import of the same record must normalize identically.
